---
import '../styles/studio.css';
import manifest from '../../public/recipe-examples/manifest.json';
import kart from '../../public/recipe-examples/blender-kart.json';
const examples = [
  {id:'lowpoly-anything',name:'Low Poly · anything',description:'Animals, creatures, objects, characters, vehicles, places or complete scenes. You choose the subject and camera.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-track-overview',name:'Low Poly · track overview',description:'A complete racing circuit from overhead, with a clear route, simple terrain and sparse supporting structures.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-character',name:'Low Poly · character reference',description:'One complete figure with simple clothing, a neutral pose and a readable silhouette.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-vehicle',name:'Low Poly · kart and vehicle reference',description:'Clear wheels, chassis, seat and large body panels on a plain background.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-prop',name:'Low Poly · prop reference',description:'One complete object with visible thicknesses, simple joins and broad material colors.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-building',name:'Low Poly · building reference',description:'A complete structure with simple roof and wall volumes, a door and clear window openings.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-diorama',name:'Low Poly · floating diorama',description:'A compact miniature scene with angular terrain and a few focal structures.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-retro',name:'Low Poly · 1990s game scene',description:'Chunky shapes, a clear silhouette and the atmosphere of an early 3D game.'},
  {id:'lowpoly-world',name:'Low Poly · landscape and game world',description:'Broad color planes, faceted terrain and readable layers of scenery.'},
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="MOSS Low Poly presets and Blender reference starters for characters, karts, objects and buildings."/><title>MOSS Low Poly — Atelier Guide</title></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/studio/">← atelier</a><span>MOSS Low Poly guide · October 31, 2026</span></header>
<main style="max-width:1100px;padding-bottom:70px">
<section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">MOSS. SIMPLE FORMS. CLEAR REFERENCES.</p><h1>Build a polygon world.</h1><p>Choose a MOSS Low Poly recipe, describe your subject and let the preset prepare the style and settings. Use Anything for a free choice of motif, or Track overview for a complete circuit from above.</p></div></section>
<section class="guide"><div><h2>Low Poly with MOSS</h2><p>MOSS covers characters, karts, objects, modular buildings and complete scenes. No additional low-poly model or style adapter is needed. Anima Aesthetic remains available for anime and illustration.</p><p>The dedicated asset recipes request large polygon faces, simple matte colors, a complete silhouette and neutral lighting. The three scene recipes retain their existing compositions.</p></div><div><h3>Settings are ready</h3><p>Recommended uses 50 Euler steps, CFG 3 and flow shift 5. Anything, Track overview and Blender-reference Draft use 30 steps at a smaller size. More detail uses 60 steps. Existing scene Draft presets use 20 steps.</p><p>Start with one subject and a few defining colors. More sampling steps do not establish geometric accuracy. Inspect the full prompt preview when you change the requested view or asset type.</p></div><div><h3>A practical brief</h3><p>Name the main volumes and how they connect. For a kart: four wheels, two axles, one seat, a simple frame and large body panels. For a character: a role, a neutral pose, simple clothing and one accessory.</p><p>Use construction notes for proportions and joins. Put a small palette and large design details into the materials field. The service supplies a plain background and even light in Blender reference mode.</p></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="examples-title"><h2 id="examples-title">MOSS examples, ready to change</h2><p>These are real local MOSS generations. Each link restores the recorded example inputs, quality and seed.</p><div class="recipe-grid">{examples.map(example=><article class="recipe-card"><img src={'/studio/recipe-examples/'+example.id+'.webp'} width="1024" height="1024" loading="lazy" alt={example.name+' generated with MOSS'}/><div class="recipe-card-body"><h3>{example.name}</h3><p>{example.description}</p><p class="hint">{manifest[example.id]?.quality==='preview'?'Draft':'Recommended'} · {manifest[example.id]?.steps} Euler steps · CFG 3</p><a class="quiet" href={'/studio/?recipe='+example.id+'#workspace'}>Try this recipe ↗</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section id="blender" aria-labelledby="blender-title" class="blender-workflow"><p class="eyebrow">FROM CONCEPT TO A SHARED 3D DESIGN</p><h2 id="blender-title">A reference you can rebuild in Blender</h2><p>Choose <strong>Blender reference</strong>, an asset type and one view. Characters use a full-body neutral pose; vehicles use a level chassis and straight wheels. “Use Blender starter” supplies an editable subject and construction brief. New asset examples already include these settings.</p>
<div class="blender-starters"><a class="quiet" href="/studio/?recipe=lowpoly-character&amp;modeling_view=three-quarter&amp;modeling_asset=character#workspace">Character starter ↗</a><a class="quiet" href="/studio/?recipe=lowpoly-vehicle&amp;modeling_view=three-quarter&amp;modeling_asset=vehicle#workspace">Kart starter ↗</a><a class="quiet" href="/studio/?recipe=lowpoly-building&amp;modeling_view=three-quarter&amp;modeling_asset=building#workspace">Building starter ↗</a><a class="quiet" href="/studio/?recipe=lowpoly-prop&amp;modeling_view=three-quarter&amp;modeling_asset=prop#workspace">Prop starter ↗</a></div>
<p><strong>A generated image is a design proposal.</strong> Independent AI views can change proportions, hidden surfaces and costume or mechanical details. A fixed seed and an orthographic prompt do not establish matched geometry. The current profiles are text-to-image models; uploading a master image does not enable a verified multi-view reconstruction workflow.</p>
<ol><li><strong>Choose one master concept.</strong> Freeze its silhouette, part list, palette and defining features. Keep the original PNG and write down the dimensions and asset budget separately.</li><li><strong>Build the large forms first.</strong> Match the concept with boxes, low-sided cylinders and planes in Blender. Use one fixed comparison camera and decide hidden geometry once in this shared blockout.</li><li><strong>Check landmarks.</strong> Compare head/body ratio, shoulders, belt and soles for characters; compare wheel centers, tire size, wheelbase, chassis width, seat and steering for vehicles.</li><li><strong>Render matched views from the same scene.</strong> Use orthographic front, side, back and top cameras, a shared origin and matching scale for views that must align. Add sheet labels, swatches and guides in the layout.</li><li><strong>Record what was checked.</strong> Compare silhouettes, dimensions and material assignments. A “PASS” badge alone does not prove geometric accuracy. Check topology, UVs and rigging on the actual mesh.</li></ol>
<p>Blender supports <a href="https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/5.0/modeling/empties.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">image empties for references</a> and <a href="https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/4.1/render/cameras.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">orthographic cameras</a>. The image presets improve readability; they do not export a mesh or guarantee a pixel-perfect reconstruction.</p></section>
{kart.model==='moss'&&<figure class="modeling-sample"><img src="/studio/recipe-examples/blender-kart.webp" width={Number(kart.size.split('x')[0])} height={Number(kart.size.split('x')[1])} loading="lazy" alt="Low-poly kart generated by MOSS on a neutral background."/><figcaption><strong>Rendered with the MOSS vehicle starter.</strong> {kart.steps} Euler steps, CFG {kart.sampling.cfg}, flow shift 5, seed {kart.seed}, {kart.size}. <a href="/studio/?recipe=lowpoly-vehicle&amp;modeling_view=three-quarter&amp;modeling_asset=vehicle#workspace">Use this starter ↗</a> · <a href="/studio/recipe-examples/blender-kart.json">Recorded settings (JSON) ↗</a></figcaption></figure>}
</main></body></html>
